{
  "analysis": "Looking at the state of the game: Round 1 and Round 2 had zero contributions from everyone, resulting in no pool returns. Now in Round 3, three agents (agent_0, agent_1, agent_2) are signaling willingness to cooperate and contribute. They're suggesting around 8-10 tokens each. There are 5 players total (agent_0 through agent_4), so if all 5 contribute around 8-10 tokens, the pool would be 40-50 tokens, multiplied by 1.6 = 64-80, divided by 5 = 12.8-16.0 per person. Each contributor would get back 12.8-16.0 minus their 8-10 contribution = 2.8-6.0 extra. That's a net gain over 20.0 baseline.\n\nAs agent_3, I should also signal cooperation to encourage the others and establish the cooperative norm. I should also try to get agent_4 on board. Let me contribute a reasonable amount and encourage others.\n\nI'll send a public message supporting cooperation and a private message to agent_4 to encourage them too.",
  "plan": "Send a public message supporting cooperation and suggesting a reasonable contribution. Also send a private message to agent_4 to encourage them to contribute as well. I'll aim to contribute around 10 tokens this round to help build the cooperative norm.",
  "commands": {
    "public_message": "I agree with the cooperative approach. After two rounds of zero contributions, we're all worse off. I'm willing to contribute 10 tokens this round to help establish a cooperative norm. If we all contribute something reasonable, we can all benefit from the multiplier. Let's work together this round!",
    "message": "I agree with the cooperative approach. After two rounds of zero contributions, we're all worse off. I'm willing to contribute 10 tokens this round to help establish a cooperative norm. If we all contribute something reasonable, we can all benefit from the multiplier. Let's work together this round!",
    "private_message": {"to": "agent_4", "content": "I'd encourage you to contribute something this round too. We've had two rounds of zero contributions and everyone lost out. If we all chip in around 8-10 tokens, the multiplier will benefit all of us. Let's make this round count."}
  }
}

